Introduction to General Knowledge: GK helps students become aware of the world around them. It covers human body, animals, plants, countries, science, space, and daily life.
Human Body and Health: The brain controls our body. The heart pumps blood. Lungs help us breathe. Importance of healthy food, exercise, and cleanliness.
Animals and Birds: Domestic animals (cows, dogs) live with humans. Wild animals (lions, tigers) live in forests.
Plants and Trees: Essential for life. Provide oxygen, food, medicine, and shelter. Types: herbs, shrubs, and trees.
Our Country – India: National flag, animal, bird, and flower. Festivals, traditions, and famous places.
The World Around Us: Continents, oceans, and seas. Earth as a planet.
Science in Daily Life: Magnets, light, sound, and energy. Day and night occurrence.
Space and the Universe: Sun, Moon, stars, and planets. Solar system. Sun is a star.
Famous People and Achievers: GK introduces students to famous people who have contributed to society. These may include leaders, scientists, writers, and sports personalities. Learning about their lives inspires students to work hard and follow good values. Stories of achievers teach students that dedication and effort lead to success.
Good Habits and Social Awareness: Cleanliness, safety rules, traffic signals, and helping others.
